# Duplicate-labelset guard on an INSTANT name-dropping function (#1839).
#
# `ceil` — like every instant math fn, the clamp family, unary minus, the
# date fns and scalar⊗vector arithmetic — drops `__name__` per PromQL's
# derived-sample rule. A selector spanning SEVERAL metrics therefore hands
# the projection two rows that differ only by name, and after the drop they
# carry ONE label set.
#
# Upstream raises the error from a generic per-step site rather than from
# `ceil` itself: rangeEval checks every output vector for a repeated label
# set (prometheus/promql/engine.go:1531, :1552) and answers "vector cannot
# contain metrics with the same labelset". #1811 wired the check into the
# RANGE half (rate / *_over_time); this is the instant half, and it is the
# same guard — an Aggregate whose HAVING carries
# `throwIf(uniqExact(MetricName) > 1, …) = 0`.
#
# The Aggregate is also the FIX and not merely the detector: without it the
# name-dropping Project leaves two identically-labelled rows on the wire,
# which the Prom response format has no shape for. Collapsing is exact
# because the HAVING has already aborted every group holding more than one
# name.
#
# Note what the guard does NOT touch: `ceil(cpu_temp)` pins one metric
# name, so no two rows can collide and the lowering keeps its unguarded,
# un-aggregated shape (see edge_ceil.txtar and friends, all byte-identical).
#
# This fixture carries no `-- seed --`: the query it pins is one that must
# FAIL, and the chDB round-trip runner has no shape for an expected error —
# the same reason rate_multi_name_duplicate_labelset_guard.txtar is
# seedless. The executable half lives at the wire, in
# internal/api/prom/handler_chdb_duplicate_labelset_test.go, which asserts
# HTTP 422 / errorType=execution / the upstream message text.
-- query.promql --
ceil({__name__=~"cpu_temp|gpu_temp"})
-- parity_exempt --
reason: rejection-only
detail: This query must be REJECTED (HTTP 422); it carries no seed/expected_rows because the round-trip runner has no shape for an expected error. The executable assertion lives in internal/api/prom/handler_chdb_duplicate_labelset_test.go, not in a value comparison RunParity could perform.
